{"chunk_id": "c-bca12f9ba03d2c84", "claim_id": "A031-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/storage-entry-size", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A031", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "For Vault deployments using the Consul storage backend, the default entry size limit is 512 KiB. The default size is enforced by Consul rather than Vault.", "span_end": 1084, "span_start": 930, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-bca12f9ba03d2c84", "claim_id": "A031-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/storage-entry-size", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A031", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "However, Consul **does not** chunk storage entries the way Vault does. Consul stores the entry as a single, large write.", "span_end": 1353, "span_start": 1233, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-bca12f9ba03d2c84", "claim_id": "A031-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/storage-entry-size", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A031", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Even small changes may result in large read-modify-write cycles for storage entries, which can degrade Vault performance. Larger writes may also destabilize your Consul cluster by delaying heartbeats, which can lead to cluster leadership instability.", "span_end": 1604, "span_start": 1354, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-cc70d28134835765", "claim_id": "A032-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/secrets/identity", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "It internally maintains the clients who are recognized by Vault. Each client is internally termed as an `Entity`. An entity can have multiple `Aliases`.", "span_end": 227, "span_start": 75, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-cc70d28134835765", "claim_id": "A032-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/secrets/identity", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "For example, a single user who has accounts in both GitHub and LDAP, can be mapped to a single entity in Vault that has 2 aliases, one of type GitHub and one of type LDAP.", "span_end": 399, "span_start": 228, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-8924b1ef2b240af8", "claim_id": "A032-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/concepts/client-count", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A032", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "In **rare** cases, tokens may be created outside of the Vault identity system **without** an associated entity or identity. Vault treats every unaffiliated token as a unique client for production usage.", "span_end": 202, "span_start": 0, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-d729ec9ab9bb9930", "claim_id": "A033-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "api-docs/system/audit-hash", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A033", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "This endpoint hashes the given input data with the specified audit device's hash function and salt. This endpoint can be used to discover whether a given plaintext string (the `input` parameter) appears in the audit log in obfuscated form.", "span_end": 525, "span_start": 286, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-ebb3121dc0539b48", "claim_id": "A033-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "partials/telemetry-metrics/vault/audit/log_request_failure", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A033", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Any increase in this counter indicates that all the configured audit devices failed to log a request (or response). If Vault cannot properly audit a request, or the response to a request, the original request will fail.", "span_end": 1181, "span_start": 962, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f208c43f780505d5", "claim_id": "A035-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/security", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A035", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When Vault is started, it starts in a _sealed_ state. This means that the encryption key needed to read and write from the storage backend is not yet known. The process of unsealing requires providing the root key so that the encryption key can be retrieved.", "span_end": 1918, "span_start": 1660, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f208c43f780505d5", "claim_id": "A035-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/security", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A035", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "The risk of distributing the root key is that a single malicious attacker with access to it can decrypt the entire Vault. Instead, Shamir's technique allows us to split the root key into multiple shares or parts.", "span_end": 2131, "span_start": 1919, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-f208c43f780505d5", "claim_id": "A035-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/security", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A035", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "By using a secret sharing technique, we avoid the need to place absolute trust in the holder of the root key, and avoid storing the root key at all. The root key is only retrievable by reconstructing the shares.", "span_end": 2509, "span_start": 2298, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-9e0778c53e40a1b4", "claim_id": "A036-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Sealing tells the Vault server to stop responding to any operations until it is unsealed.", "span_end": 133, "span_start": 44, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-9e0778c53e40a1b4", "claim_id": "A036-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "When sealed, the Vault server discards its in-memory root key to unlock the data, so it is physically blocked from responding to operations unsealed.", "span_end": 283, "span_start": 134, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-9e0778c53e40a1b4", "claim_id": "A036-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/commands/operator/seal", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A036", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "If an unseal is in progress, sealing the Vault will reset the unsealing process.", "span_end": 365, "span_start": 285, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-d2d0a828a972d7ae", "claim_id": "A037-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/configuration/prevent-lease-explosions", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Lease explosions can occur when a Vault cluster is over-subscribed and clients overwhelm system resources with consistent, high-volume API requests", "span_end": 244, "span_start": 97, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-d2d0a828a972d7ae", "claim_id": "A037-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/configuration/prevent-lease-explosions", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Unchecked lease explosions create a memory drain on the active node, which can cascade to other nodes and result in denial-of-service issues for the entire cluster.", "span_end": 410, "span_start": 246, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-d2d0a828a972d7ae", "claim_id": "A037-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/configuration/prevent-lease-explosions", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A037", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "High lease counts can degrade system performance:", "span_end": 1628, "span_start": 1579, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-83d6d5073feb7cd0", "claim_id": "A040-c1", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/security", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A040", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "This means that data at rest and in transit must be secure from eavesdropping or tampering.", "span_end": 391, "span_start": 300, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-83d6d5073feb7cd0", "claim_id": "A040-c2", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/security", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A040", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Clients must be appropriately authenticated and authorized to access data or modify policies.", "span_end": 485, "span_start": 392, "supported": true}
{"chunk_id": "c-83d6d5073feb7cd0", "claim_id": "A040-c3", "containment_ok": true, "detail": "", "doc_id": "docs/internals/security", "error_class": "", "item_id": "A040", "judge_reason": "", "judge_supported": null, "nli_score": null, "nli_supported": null, "quote": "Client communication with Vault should be secure from eavesdropping as well as communication from Vault to its storage backend or between Vault cluster nodes.", "span_end": 952, "span_start": 790, "supported": true}
